>What _is_ a grid bug anyway?

It's a creature from Tron. :-)

Tron was a movie that came out around 1981 right smack in the middle of the
first video game boom.   The main character entered the "world of the
computer" via a prototype transporter, to defeat the evil Master Control
Program, running through basically a fantasy world where programs were people
and things.  The movie had some computer animation in it, and lots of fake
"computer animation" done by recoloring normal scenes.  There was an associated
video game, with four parts based on scenes from the movie.

The main grid bug scene apparently was cut from the movie, but stayed in the
game.  In it, grid bugs are cannon fodder which you shoot a path through; you
then spend the rest of the scene blasting them for points.  They only move
along grid lines (tilted diagonally in the game).  They weren't green in the
game, though I don't know about the movie.
